From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] audio: aidl: primary: add vendor capture hook for multi-channel microphone array processing

Built-in 4-microphone array processing (beamforming, echo cancellation, and NPU
denoise) requires opening the underlying ALSA capture PCM in 4-channel mode
while delivering processed 2-channel frames to the client, along with access
to the active AudioSource metadata and capture timestamp latency compensation.

Add an optional vendor capture hook to StreamAlsaBase / StreamAlsaMonoPipe /
StreamPrimary configured via ro.vendor.audio.primary.capture_hook:
- Query capture_hook_open() before opening built-in ALSA capture proxies so the
  hook can override the hardware channel count and report its processing delay;
- Transform each captured hardware PCM block via capture_hook_process() in the
  capture I/O thread before writing into the MonoPipe;
- Forward SinkMetadata AudioSource updates via capture_hook_set_sources();
- Subtract the hook's processing delay in refinePosition().

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [device-specific DSP hook]
---
